    <string name="guide_title_ph">pH Probe: Calibration Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_title_temp">Temperature Sensor: Calibration Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_title_salinity">Salinity / Conductivity: Calibration Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_title_ammonia">Ammonia Probe: Calibration Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_title_do2">Dissolved O₂ Probe: Calibration Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_ph">1. Rinse probe with distilled water.\n2. Submerge in pH 7 buffer solution for 60 seconds.\n3. Rinse again, then submerge in pH 4 (or pH 10) buffer for 60 seconds.\n4. Rinse thoroughly. Probe is ready.</string>
    <string name="guide_temp">1. Place sensor in a verified ice-water bath (0 °C / 32 °F).\n2. Wait 60 seconds for reading to stabilise.\n3. Repeat with boiling water (100 °C / 212 °F) if possible.\n4. Note any offset and adjust in your controller if needed.</string>
    <string name="guide_salinity">1. Rinse probe with distilled water.\n2. Submerge in a certified seawater reference solution (e.g. 35 ppt).\n3. Wait 30 seconds and verify the reading matches the solution value.\n4. Rinse with distilled water after use.</string>
    <string name="guide_ammonia">1. Use 0 ppm and 2 ppm NH₃ standard solutions.\n2. Rinse probe with distilled water between measurements.\n3. Submerge in each solution for 60 seconds.\n4. Allow full stabilisation before recording values.</string>
    <string name="guide_do2">1. Expose the membrane cap to open air for 120 seconds (100% saturation reference).\n2. Optionally use a 0% saturation solution (sodium sulfite) for zero calibration.\n3. Rinse membrane with distilled water before returning to tank.</string>
